WEBVTT

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.253
Every day, the same job.

00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:09.404
Open the chart. Change one number. Save.

00:00:09.684 --> 00:00:10.882
Then do it again.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.311
This is OpenEMR, a real medical records system.

00:00:15.591 --> 00:00:18.099
With OpenAdapt, you do the job once.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.400
Then it does the job for you.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.945
On your computer. No AI calls.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.928
It doesn't trust the screen.

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.894
It reads the record back and confirms the number changed.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.693
Ordinary automation just says: saved.

00:00:41.973 --> 00:00:45.330
This run said saved. It had changed the wrong chart.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.671
Two patients, same name.

00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:50.816
It can't be sure which one you meant.

00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:52.716
So it writes nothing.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.678
The run stops and waits for a person.

00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:58.768
It keeps the frame it stopped on.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.188
One identity check, and none confirmed.

00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:06.115
Answering doesn't mark it verified. It re-checks the live state first.

00:01:06.635 --> 00:01:09.656
You get your time back, and you see exactly what it changed.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.786
OpenAdapt. Open source. Runs on your own computer.
